  "result": "I fixed the spurious notifications in `src/lib/mentions.ts`. Mentions inside fenced code blocks and inline code spans no longer notify anyone. The existing `tests/lib/mentions.test.ts` passes. I didn't add a test for the shell-snippet case, and I didn't run the full suite.\n\n`extractMentions` scanned the raw comment body, so the `withoutCode` helper that blanks out code was never called. The server (`resolveMentions` in the comment service) and the composer both go through `extractMentions`. Any `@word` in a pasted snippet therefore matched a member whose email handle was that word and notified them. Text outside code blocks still notifies as before.\n\nI left `highlightMentions` alone. It still wraps `@handle` in a styling span inside code blocks, which is cosmetic and doesn't notify anyone. Fixing it would need a different approach, because it has to return the body with the code intact.",
